# Physics-Based Character System (6DOF Joint) — Implementation Plan

Replace Trunk2026's `CharacterVirtual` ghost-body character with a **real physics-based character** inspired by Trunk2016's [Motor6D](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/v8datamodel/JointInstance.h#288-289) / [Humanoid](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/humanoid/Humanoid.h#274-275) architecture.

## Current vs Target Architecture

### Current System (Trunk2026)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["CharacterController (Instance)"] -->|"owns handle"| B["JPH::CharacterVirtual (ghost)"]
    A -->|"drives"| C["CharacterControllerComponent"]
    D["PlayerCharacter"] -->|"reads position from"| A
    D -->|"BoneAttachment"| E["Part Entities (Head, Torso, Arms, Legs)"]
    E -->|"animation-driven only"| F["AnimatorSystem + HierarchySystem"]
    B -.->|"NO real body, NO collisions with other players"| G["Jolt Physics World"]
```

> [!WARNING]
> The current `CharacterVirtual` is a **ghost**: it queries contacts but has **no physics body** in the broadphase. Other characters cannot collide with it. Body parts are purely visual, positioned by animation bones.

### Target System (Trunk2016-inspired)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["CharacterController (Instance)"] -->|"owns"| B["JPH::Character (real body)"]
    B -->|"RootPart body"| C["Jolt Physics World"]
    A -->|"applies forces"| B
    D["Motor6DJoint (6DOF)"] -->|"connects"| E["RootPart ↔ Head"]
    D2["Motor6DJoint"] -->|"connects"| F["RootPart ↔ UpperTorso"]
    D3["Motor6DJoint"] -->|"connects"| G["RootPart ↔ LeftArm"]
    D4["Motor6DJoint"] -->|"connects"| H["RootPart ↔ RightArm"]
    D5["Motor6DJoint"] -->|"connects"| I["RootPart ↔ LeftLeg"]
    D6["Motor6DJoint"] -->|"connects"| J["RootPart ↔ RightLeg"]
    E & F & G & H & I & J -->|"per-part bodies"| C
    K["Animator"] -->|"applyPose()"| D & D2 & D3 & D4 & D5 & D6
```

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Trunk2016 Approach | Our Approach |
|---|---|---|
| Root body | Custom physics engine body via [Primitive](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/humanoid/Humanoid.cpp#2776-2784) | `JPH::Character` (real Jolt body — has mass, collides) |
| Limb bodies | Full physics [Primitive](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/humanoid/Humanoid.cpp#2776-2784) per part | `JPH::Body` (kinematic, positioned by joints) |
| Joint type | [Motor6DJoint](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/v8world/Motor6DJoint.h#9-59) using custom `D6Link` | [Motor6DJoint](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/v8world/Motor6DJoint.h#9-59) wrapper around `JPH::SixDOFConstraint` |
| Movement forces | `Humanoid::computeForce()` via KernelJoint | `CharacterController::Update()` — applies linear velocity to `JPH::Character` |
| Animation | `Motor6DJoint::applyPose()` sets offset+axisAngle | Same pattern: `Motor6DJoint::ApplyPose()` sets 6DOF target transforms |
| Ground detection | Custom floor plane contact | `JPH::Character::GetGroundState()` |

## Proposed Changes

### PhysicsWorld — Real Character Body + 6DOF Constraints

#### [MODIFY] [PhysicsWorld.h](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Physics/PhysicsWorld.h)

- Add `#include <Jolt/Physics/Character/Character.h>` and `#include <Jolt/Physics/Constraints/SixDOFConstraint.h>`
- Change `std::unordered_map<int, JPH::CharacterVirtual*> m_Characters` → `std::unordered_map<int, JPH::Character*> m_Characters`
- Add new APIs:
  - `uint32_t AddDynamicBody(...)` — creates a kinematic body for limbs
  - `void AddSixDOFConstraint(uint32_t bodyA, uint32_t bodyB, ...)` — creates a 6DOF constraint between two bodies
  - `void SetSixDOFTarget(constraintHandle, offset, rotation)` — drives joint target for animation

#### [MODIFY] [PhysicsWorld.cpp](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp)

- **[AddCharacter()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp#234-282)**: Replace `JPH::CharacterVirtual` with `JPH::Character`:
  - Creates a **real** `JPH::Body` with a box shape (matching RootPart dimensions)
  - Uses `JPH::CharacterSettings` instead of `JPH::CharacterVirtualSettings`
  - Body lives in the `CHARACTER` layer, collides with `NON_MOVING`, `MOVING`, and `CHARACTER` (enabling player-to-player collision)
- **`UpdateCharacter()`**: Use `JPH::Character::SetLinearVelocity()` instead of `CharacterVirtual::ExtendedUpdate()` (simpler, as Jolt handles all contact resolution for real bodies)
- **`AddDynamicBody()`**: New function — creates a kinematic body for each limb part (lightweight, animation-positioned)
- **`AddSixDOFConstraint()`**: New function — creates `JPH::SixDOFConstraint` between RootPart body and each limb body, with configurable axis locks and motor targets
- **`SetSixDOFTarget()`**: New function — sets motor target position/rotation on a `SixDOFConstraint` (called by animation system to pose joints)
- **Collision layers**: Update `ObjectLayerPairFilterImpl::ShouldCollide()` to allow `CHARACTER ↔ CHARACTER` collisions

---

### Motor6DJoint — New Data Model Class

#### [NEW] [Motor6DJoint.h](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Motor6DJoint.h)

New [Instance](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Instance.h#16-102)-derived class representing a 6DOF joint between two Parts:

```cpp
class Motor6DJoint : public Instance {
public:
    Motor6DJoint(entt::registry& registry);

    // -- Joint Definition --
    void SetPart0(Instance* part);  // Parent body
    void SetPart1(Instance* part);  // Child body
    Instance* GetPart0() const;
    Instance* GetPart1() const;

    void SetC0(const glm::mat4& offset);  // Offset in Part0's space
    void SetC1(const glm::mat4& offset);  // Offset in Part1's space
    glm::mat4 GetC0() const;
    glm::mat4 GetC1() const;

    // -- Animation Interface --
    void ApplyPose(const glm::vec3& offset, const glm::quat& rotation, float weight);
    
    // -- Physics Binding --
    void InitPhysics(PhysicsWorld* physics);
    void ShutdownPhysics();
    void Update(float dt);  // Drives constraint motor targets from current pose

    // -- Pose State --
    glm::vec3 GetCurrentOffset() const;
    glm::quat GetCurrentRotation() const;

    // -- MaxVelocity (legacy compat) --
    void SetMaxVelocity(float vel);
    float GetMaxVelocity() const;
};
```

#### [NEW] [Motor6DJoint.cpp](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Motor6DJoint.cpp)

Implementation:
- [InitPhysics()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#213-222): Creates `SixDOFConstraint` via `PhysicsWorld::AddSixDOFConstraint()` using body IDs from Part0 and Part1
- `ApplyPose()`: Stores target offset+rotation with weight blending, similar to Trunk2016's `Motor6DJoint::applyPose()`
- [Update()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#241-334): Interpolates current pose towards target, calls `PhysicsWorld::SetSixDOFTarget()` to drive the constraint motors
- Pose freshness tracking (32-frame timeout, fade-back) matching Trunk2016's `poseFreshness` / `poseDuration` pattern

---

### Motor6DJointComponent — ECS Component

#### [NEW] [Motor6DJointComponent.h](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/Components/Motor6DJointComponent.h)

```cpp
struct Motor6DJointComponent {
    entt::entity Part0 = entt::null;
    entt::entity Part1 = entt::null;
    glm::mat4 C0 = glm::mat4(1.0f);
    glm::mat4 C1 = glm::mat4(1.0f);

    // Animation pose state
    glm::vec3 CurrentOffset = glm::vec3(0);
    glm::quat CurrentRotation = glm::quat(1, 0, 0, 0);
    glm::vec3 TargetOffset = glm::vec3(0);
    glm::quat TargetRotation = glm::quat(1, 0, 0, 0);
    float PoseWeight = 1.0f;
    float PoseMaskWeight = 1.0f;
    int PoseFreshness = 0;

    // Physics handle
    int ConstraintHandle = -1;
    float MaxVelocity = 0.1f;
};
```

