### CharacterController — Use Real Physics Body

#### [MODIFY] [CharacterController.h](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.h)

- Add:
  - `std::vector<Motor6DJoint*> m_Joints` — list of joints connecting character parts
  - `void BuildJoints(PhysicsWorld* physics)` — creates Motor6DJoint for each Part in the character Model
  - `void UpdateJoints(float dt)` — ticks all joints (drives motor targets from animation)
  - `std::vector<uint32_t> m_LimbBodyIDs` — Jolt body IDs for limb parts
- No change to the public API (SetWalkSpeed, Jump, etc. remain the same)

#### [MODIFY] [CharacterController.cpp](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp)

- **[InitPhysics()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#213-222)**: After calling `PhysicsWorld::AddCharacter()`, iterate the character Model's children (Parts), and for each:
  - Call `PhysicsWorld::AddDynamicBody()` to create a kinematic body
  - Create a [Motor6DJoint](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/v8world/Motor6DJoint.h#9-59) connecting RootPart → each limb Part
  - Call `Motor6DJoint::InitPhysics()` to create the SixDOFConstraint
- **[Update()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#241-334)**: After the existing velocity/state logic:
  - Call `UpdateJoints()` to tick all Motor6DJoint instances
- **[ShutdownPhysics()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#223-230)**: Clean up limb bodies and joints

---

### PlayerCharacter — Wire Up 6DOF Assembly

#### [MODIFY] [PlayerCharacter.h](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Character/PlayerCharacter.h)

- No structural changes needed. The existing `m_Controller` already owns the physics logic. The Motor6DJoint creation happens inside `CharacterController::InitPhysics()`.

#### [MODIFY] [PlayerCharacter.cpp](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Character/PlayerCharacter.cpp)

- **[Spawn()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/Character/PlayerCharacter.cpp#58-177)**: After calling `m_Controller->InitPhysics()`, the controller now automatically creates joints. No major changes needed.
- **[Update()](file:///F:/Trunk2026/Source/Runtime/Core/DataModel/CharacterController.cpp#241-334)**: The animator system drives bone transforms → `BoneAttachmentComponent` provides target transforms → `Motor6DJoint::ApplyPose()` drives the physics constraints. We add a step that reads animated bone transforms and pushes them into the Motor6D joints via `ApplyPose()`.

