## System Flow — How It All Works Together

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant PC as PlayerCharacter
    participant CC as CharacterController
    participant PW as PhysicsWorld
    participant M6D as Motor6DJoint
    participant Anim as AnimatorSystem

    PC->>CC: InitPhysics()
    CC->>PW: AddCharacter() [creates JPH::Character for RootPart]
    CC->>PW: AddDynamicBody() × N [creates kinematic body per limb]
    CC->>M6D: new Motor6DJoint(RootPart, LimbPart)
    M6D->>PW: AddSixDOFConstraint(rootBodyID, limbBodyID)
    
    Note over PC,PW: Every frame:
    
    PC->>CC: Move(direction) + Update(dt)
    CC->>PW: SetLinearVelocity on Character body
    PW->>PW: Step() — real physics collision + constraint solving
    CC->>CC: Read position from JPH::Character
    
    Anim->>Anim: Evaluate bone transforms
    Anim->>M6D: ApplyPose(offset, rotation, weight)
    M6D->>PW: SetSixDOFTarget(constraint, targetTransform)
    PW->>PW: Constraint motors drive limb bodies to animated pose
```

## Verification Plan

### Build Verification

Command to validate the project builds:
```
cmake --build build --config Release --target NovinteraService Player Editor
```
Run from `F:\Trunk2026`. All targets must compile without errors.

### Manual Verification

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Since there are no automated tests for the character system, verification is manual. The user should test the following after building:

1. **Launch the Player executable** and ensure the character spawns at the spawn point
2. **Walk with WASD** — character should move smoothly, with the root body sliding along the ground
3. **Jump with Space** — character should jump and fall back with gravity
4. **Check collisions** — walk into a wall; the character should stop (not pass through). If a second player is present, they should collide with each other
5. **Check limb attachment** — arms, legs, head should stay attached and follow the animation. They should NOT detach or fly away
6. **Check animation** — idle and walk animations should play correctly, with limbs moving naturally
7. **Check ragdoll** (if enabled) — when the character dies, joints should release and the body should ragdoll naturally

I will also add a **basic smoke test** that verifies the [Motor6DJoint](file:///F:/VintaBlox/Trunk2016/App/include/v8world/Motor6DJoint.h#9-59) class can be instantiated and its properties set/get correctly. This will be a simple C++ unit in a scratch file, not a full test framework integration.
